  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R1-015$qb$, $qb$A1-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You receive a message that makes you angry just before a meeting. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Pause, settle your reaction, and respond after checking the facts$qb$, $qb$Take a short break before deciding whether a reply is needed$qb$, $qb$Reply briefly so the issue does not stay unresolved$qb$, $qb$Tell a coworker how unreasonable the message was$qb$, $qb$Send your first response while the issue is fresh$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R5-015$qb$, $qb$A1-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague criticizes your idea and you feel an urge to interrupt. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Let them finish, notice your reaction, and answer the substance of the criticism$qb$, $qb$Listen fully and ask one question before replying$qb$, $qb$Interrupt briefly to correct a factual point$qb$, $qb$Stay silent even when it is your turn to respond$qb$, $qb$Interrupt so your idea is not misunderstood$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-0TO2-R6-015$qb$, $qb$A1-04$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You receive unexpected criticism during a busy day and notice you are distracted afterward. What is the best response?$qb$, $qb$Pause, separate useful feedback from emotion, and return to the next priority$qb$, $qb$Take a short break and note any useful point from the feedback$qb$, $qb$Keep working while replaying the criticism in your mind$qb$, $qb$Send a defensive reply before you forget the details$qb$, $qb$Avoid the person who gave the feedback$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
