  ($qb$HEAIL-ADP-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A1-09$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a care worker. Your employer has changed the visit schedule so you have less time with each client. One client in particular needs longer. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Set out what that client needs and ask for her visit to be reviewed$qb$, $qb$Raise with your supervisor that the new times are too short$qb$, $qb$Ask whether the schedule can be adjusted for some clients$qb$, $qb$Give that client the time she needs and run late$qb$, $qb$Follow the new schedule, since it applies to everyone$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ADP-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A1-09$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are an office administrator of twenty years. Your department is moving to a system you have never used, and the training is a single afternoon. How do you approach it?$qb$, $qb$Work out which of your tasks the system changes, and learn those first$qb$, $qb$Attend the training and ask questions about what is unclear$qb$, $qb$Ask whether more training could be arranged$qb$, $qb$Learn it as you go once the system is live$qb$, $qb$Ask to keep using the current system for your own work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ADP-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A1-09$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a small team. Your company has announced a restructure that will affect your team but the details are not settled. Your team is asking you what it means. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell them what is known, what is not, and when you expect to know more$qb$, $qb$Tell them what has been announced and that details will follow$qb$, $qb$Tell them not to worry until the details are settled$qb$, $qb$Tell them what you personally think is likely to happen$qb$, $qb$Say nothing until you have the full picture$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ADP-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A1-09$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a chef. The restaurant owner has changed suppliers and the new ingredients are not the same quality. Your dishes are affected. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Show him a dish made both ways and let him taste the difference$qb$, $qb$Tell him the new ingredients are affecting the food$qb$, $qb$Adjust the recipes to work with what you now have$qb$, $qb$Ask whether the old supplier could be used for some items$qb$, $qb$Carry on, since the supplier decision was not yours$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ADP-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A1-09$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a driver. Your route has been reorganised by a planning system and now makes less sense to you than the old one. You know the area well. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Record where the new route loses time and give that to the planner$qb$, $qb$Tell your supervisor the new route is not efficient$qb$, $qb$Follow the new route and see whether it works out$qb$, $qb$Drive your own route and complete the same deliveries$qb$, $qb$Follow the new route without comment, since it is set centrally$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ADP-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A1-09$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work on a helpdesk. A new script has been introduced for handling calls. It works for most calls but not for one common type. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Show your team leader the call type it does not fit$qb$, $qb$Raise with your team leader that the script has a gap$qb$, $qb$Use the script where it fits and improvise where it does not$qb$, $qb$Use your own approach for that type of call$qb$, $qb$Follow the script on every call as instructed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-ADP-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A1-09$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a nurse. A new handover procedure has been introduced that takes longer but is meant to reduce errors. Staff are cutting it short when the ward is busy. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Raise what is being missed when it is cut short, and what would make it workable$qb$, $qb$Raise with the ward manager that the procedure is being shortened$qb$, $qb$Follow the full procedure yourself regardless of how busy it is$qb$, $qb$Ask whether a shorter version could be approved for busy periods$qb$, $qb$Do what the others do, since the ward has to keep running$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
