  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-FIB-014$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$A handover that happens in a corridor will be remembered like a ______.$qb$, $qb$conversation$qb$, $qb$meeting$qb$, $qb$record$qb$, $qb$briefing$qb$, $qb$reminder$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Work shared without a clear owner tends to be done ______.$qb$, $qb$twice$qb$, $qb$well$qb$, $qb$early$qb$, $qb$quietly$qb$, $qb$cheaply$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-016$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$On a team, which is usually the hardest thing for someone to do?$qb$, $qb$Say you are struggling with something$qb$, $qb$Point out a problem in someone else's work$qb$, $qb$Offer help to someone who has not asked for it$qb$, $qb$Take on extra work when the team is behind$qb$, $qb$Thank someone publicly for their help$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-017$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have finished your part of a shared job early. What is the most useful thing to do?$qb$, $qb$Ask what is holding up the parts still to be done$qb$, $qb$Offer your help to whoever seems busiest$qb$, $qb$Check your own work again while you wait$qb$, $qb$Start on the next job on your own list$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager you have finished$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague on your team is not pulling his weight and others are covering. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Speak to him about what you have been picking up$qb$, $qb$Raise it with the whole team as a shared problem$qb$, $qb$Raise it with your manager$qb$, $qb$Keep covering and wait for someone else to raise it$qb$, $qb$Stop covering so the gap becomes visible$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team is behind and everyone is working flat out. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out which part everything else is waiting on$qb$, $qb$Work faster on your own part$qb$, $qb$Ask for more people to be added$qb$, $qb$Ask which parts could be dropped$qb$, $qb$Work longer hours until the backlog clears$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You disagree with the way your team has decided to do something. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say so now, then support whatever the team decides$qb$, $qb$Ask for one more discussion before it is settled$qb$, $qb$Go along with it and raise it if it fails$qb$, $qb$Do your own part your own way$qb$, $qb$Say nothing, since the decision is made$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A new person has joined your team. What is most useful in the first week?$qb$, $qb$Tell her the things nobody writes down$qb$, $qb$Show her how the main tasks are done$qb$, $qb$Introduce her to everyone she will work with$qb$, $qb$Give her the written procedures to read$qb$, $qb$Let her settle in and ask questions$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably makes a group work well together?$qb$, $qb$Everyone knowing what the others are doing$qb$, $qb$Everyone getting on with each other$qb$, $qb$Everyone being good at their own job$qb$, $qb$Everyone having clear instructions$qb$, $qb$Everyone being treated fairly$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have information that would help another team but nobody has asked for it. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Send it to them and say why it may matter$qb$, $qb$Mention it to them next time you speak$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager they may find it useful$qb$, $qb$Wait until they ask for it$qb$, $qb$Keep it, since it is your team's work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team is praised for something you did most of the work on. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Accept it and name what each person contributed$qb$, $qb$Accept it on behalf of the team$qb$, $qb$Mention your own contribution to your manager afterwards$qb$, $qb$Say nothing, since the praise went to the team$qb$, $qb$Say in the moment that you did most of the work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two members of your team keep duplicating each other's work. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out how the overlap started$qb$, $qb$Agree between them who does what$qb$, $qb$Tell them they are duplicating$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager to allocate the work$qb$, $qb$Let them sort it out between themselves$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague has made a mistake that will affect your work. He has not mentioned it. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Tell him what you have found and ask what happened$qb$, $qb$Fix it and mention it to him afterwards$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager so it can be dealt with$qb$, $qb$Fix it yourself and say nothing$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since it is his mistake to fix$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to work with someone you find difficult. What matters most?$qb$, $qb$Agreeing at the start how you will work together$qb$, $qb$Keeping the working relationship professional$qb$, $qb$Being clear about who does which part$qb$, $qb$Avoiding the subjects you disagree about$qb$, $qb$Getting the work done with least contact$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens when a team has no agreed way of handing work over?$qb$, $qb$Things get lost between people rather than within them$qb$, $qb$Work takes longer than it needs to$qb$, $qb$People do more than they need to$qb$, $qb$Mistakes are harder to trace$qb$, $qb$Nobody is sure who is responsible$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your part of a job depends on another team who are running late. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask what they need to unblock it$qb$, $qb$Ask them when they now expect to finish$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager you are being held up$qb$, $qb$Work on something else until they finish$qb$, $qb$Chase them daily until it is done$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A team member has a much better idea than yours halfway through your plan. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Switch to hers and say why$qb$, $qb$Compare the two and let the team choose$qb$, $qb$Finish yours and use hers next time$qb$, $qb$Adopt the parts of hers that fit yours$qb$, $qb$Continue with yours, since the plan is agreed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You notice that one person does all the unpopular tasks on your team. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Raise how the tasks are shared, not who is doing them$qb$, $qb$Offer to take some of them yourself$qb$, $qb$Ask her whether she minds doing them$qb$, $qb$Raise it with your manager$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since she has not complained$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A group decision was made while you were absent. You think it is wrong. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Find out the reasoning before saying anything$qb$, $qb$Say you think the decision is wrong$qb$, $qb$Ask for the decision to be discussed again$qb$, $qb$Follow it, since you were not there$qb$, $qb$Follow it and say nothing about your view$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is most useful to establish at the start of a shared piece of work?$qb$, $qb$Who is responsible for each part and when it is needed$qb$, $qb$What the finished result should look like$qb$, $qb$How often the group will meet$qb$, $qb$What each person's strengths are$qb$, $qb$Who is leading the work overall$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague asks for your help when you are already stretched. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Tell him what you can do and by when$qb$, $qb$Ask him how urgent it is before agreeing$qb$, $qb$Agree and fit it in somehow$qb$, $qb$Tell him you are too busy$qb$, $qb$Agree and tell him if you cannot manage it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team's meetings always overrun and nothing is decided. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Agree what each meeting has to decide before it starts$qb$, $qb$Set a finish time and stop at it$qb$, $qb$Ask why the meetings overrun$qb$, $qb$Have fewer people at the meetings$qb$, $qb$Circulate decisions afterwards in writing$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have spotted a problem in another person's part of the work. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Tell him directly and say what you have seen$qb$, $qb$Ask him about that part without saying why$qb$, $qb$Tell whoever is coordinating the work$qb$, $qb$Fix it yourself if you are able to$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since it is not your part$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You crew a ferry. The deckhand on your shift has started leaving ten minutes before the end of each crossing to change, which means the ropes are handled by one person instead of two. Nobody has said anything. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Tell him you need him on the ropes and ask what the rush is$qb$, $qb$Tell him he must stay until the crossing is finished$qb$, $qb$Raise it with the skipper as a crewing matter$qb$, $qb$Manage the ropes alone and say nothing$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the crossings have been completed safely$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You play in an amateur football club. One player consistently misses training but plays every match because he is good. Other players have started missing training too. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Raise with the team what training is for, not who is missing it$qb$, $qb$Raise it with the manager as a fairness question$qb$, $qb$Ask the player why he does not attend training$qb$, $qb$Miss training yourself, since it seems optional$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since the team is still winning matches$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a radio taxi control room. A colleague on the other shift leaves the job log half completed, so your shift starts by working out what happened. It has happened for weeks. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Speak to him about what the gaps cost your shift$qb$, $qb$Raise it with the shift supervisor$qb$, $qb$Ask him whether something makes the log hard to complete$qb$, $qb$Complete the log yourself at the start of each shift$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since your shift manages to work it out$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are a musician in an orchestra. Your section leader takes a passage at a tempo you think is wrong. The conductor has not commented. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Play with the section and raise the tempo in rehearsal$qb$, $qb$Ask the section leader about the tempo after rehearsal$qb$, $qb$Play it at the tempo you think is correct$qb$, $qb$Ask another player in the section what they think$qb$, $qb$Ask the conductor which tempo he wants$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You volunteer with a mountain rescue team. On a callout, one volunteer wants to take a faster route that the team leader has ruled out. He is asking others to back him. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Say the team goes together on the agreed route, and settle it afterwards$qb$, $qb$Tell him the leader has already decided the route$qb$, $qb$Ask him why he thinks the other route is better$qb$, $qb$Stay out of it and follow whichever route is taken$qb$, $qb$Support him, since a faster route may matter here$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at a wholesale flower market. Your stall shares a cold store with three others. One trader regularly leaves his stock blocking the door. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Raise it with all four of you, since the store is shared$qb$, $qb$Speak to him directly about the blocked door$qb$, $qb$Move his stock out of the way each time$qb$, $qb$Raise it with the market manager$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since everyone manages to get past$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a rice mill. Your team is paid a bonus on shift output. One member works more slowly than the rest and the bonus has been missed twice. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Find out what slows him down before treating it as effort$qb$, $qb$Raise the missed bonus with the team as a whole$qb$, $qb$Speak to him about the pace he is working at$qb$, $qb$Raise it with the supervisor to deal with$qb$, $qb$Work faster yourselves to make up the difference$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You are on a film crew. The sound recordist and the camera operator each want the actor to stand somewhere different. Shooting starts in five minutes and neither will give way. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Ask what each of them needs, since a third position may work$qb$, $qb$Ask the director to decide between them$qb$, $qb$Suggest they take one shot each way$qb$, $qb$Support whichever of them has the stronger case$qb$, $qb$Stay out of it, since it is not your department$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work on a cardamom estate. Pickers are paid by weight, and the estate's grade affects what everyone is paid. One group has started picking unripe pods to increase their weight. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Raise what the lower grade costs everyone, not just what they did$qb$, $qb$Sort out the unripe pods before they are weighed$qb$, $qb$Tell them they are picking unripe pods$qb$, $qb$Report it to the estate manager$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since they are paid on their own weight$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in ambulance dispatch. A colleague on your desk has stopped passing on information she considers minor. Twice this has meant crews arrived unprepared. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Show her the two calls and what the crews were missing$qb$, $qb$Tell her that all information needs passing on$qb$, $qb$Ask her how she decides what is minor$qb$, $qb$Pass on the information yourself when you notice$qb$, $qb$Report the two incidents to the supervisor$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
