  ($qb$HEAIL-TMC-SJT-048$qb$, $qb$A1-06$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a potters' collective. One member's pieces are consistently below the standard the collective is known for, and they go out under the shared mark. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Raise it as a question about the shared mark, with the whole collective$qb$, $qb$Speak to him about the standard of his pieces$qb$, $qb$Ask him whether he wants help with the technique$qb$, $qb$Sort his pieces out before they go to market$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since each member works independently$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
