  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Feedback you never ask for is feedback you receive only when something has ______.$qb$, $qb$gone wrong$qb$, $qb$been repeated$qb$, $qb$been delayed$qb$, $qb$been counted$qb$, $qb$been approved$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-FIB-017$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Knowing what your manager will be asked about next week tells you what to have ______.$qb$, $qb$ready$qb$, $qb$cheaper$qb$, $qb$shorter$qb$, $qb$newer$qb$, $qb$quieter$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager has given you two tasks, both due tomorrow. Together they need more hours than you have. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say both cannot be done by tomorrow and ask which comes first$qb$, $qb$Ask which of the two is more important$qb$, $qb$Start the one that takes longer and see how far you get$qb$, $qb$Do both quickly and accept that neither will be thorough$qb$, $qb$Do the one you were given first and explain later$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You disagree with an instruction from your manager. When is the best time to say so?$qb$, $qb$Before you start, while the instruction can still change$qb$, $qb$As soon as you have thought it through properly$qb$, $qb$After you have tried it and can show the problem$qb$, $qb$At the next scheduled meeting with her$qb$, $qb$Once the work is finished and the result is clear$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager is judged on targets of her own. Which part of that is worth knowing?$qb$, $qb$Which of your tasks feed into them$qb$, $qb$The way those targets are measured$qb$, $qb$When she is next asked about them$qb$, $qb$Who set the targets in the first place$qb$, $qb$How demanding the targets are$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager asks how a piece of work is going and it is behind. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say how far behind and what would bring it back$qb$, $qb$Say it is behind and explain what caused it$qb$, $qb$Give her a new date you are confident of$qb$, $qb$Say it is nearly there and push to catch up$qb$, $qb$Say it is on track and hope to recover the time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A senior manager has asked you directly to do something. Your own manager does not know. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Tell your manager today, before the work starts$qb$, $qb$Do the work and tell your manager afterwards$qb$, $qb$Ask the senior manager to speak to your manager$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager whether you should do it$qb$, $qb$Do it, since the request came from someone senior$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually happens when someone agrees to every request from their manager?$qb$, $qb$The manager loses sight of what the person can actually carry$qb$, $qb$The person becomes overloaded and misses deadlines$qb$, $qb$The quality of the work falls$qb$, $qb$The manager gives them more work than others$qb$, $qb$The person becomes resentful over time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager has changed a priority for the third time this month. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find out what keeps changing upstream of her$qb$, $qb$Ask her to confirm the current priority in writing$qb$, $qb$Ask why the priority keeps changing$qb$, $qb$Follow the latest instruction and say nothing$qb$, $qb$Carry on with the original priority until told again$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager has given you something you believe belongs to another team. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Do it, and tell her where you think it properly sits$qb$, $qb$Ask her whether it should have come to you$qb$, $qb$Do it without raising the question$qb$, $qb$Suggest she passes it to the other team$qb$, $qb$Decline it, since it is not your team's work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager gives instructions you often find unclear. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say back what you understood and let her correct it$qb$, $qb$Ask her to be more specific when she gives them$qb$, $qb$Ask questions until you are sure$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague what she usually means$qb$, $qb$Do your best and check the result with her$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the main risk of solving a problem without telling your manager it happened?$qb$, $qb$She cannot stop it happening elsewhere$qb$, $qb$She may have had a better solution$qb$, $qb$She may hear about it from someone else$qb$, $qb$The same problem may return$qb$, $qb$You get no credit for solving it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager praises work you know contains a mistake she has not seen. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Tell her about the mistake now$qb$, $qb$Correct it and tell her it is corrected$qb$, $qb$Tell her at the next opportunity$qb$, $qb$Correct it quietly and say nothing$qb$, $qb$Leave it, since she is satisfied with the work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are asked to do something you believe is a waste of time. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Ask what it is meant to produce before deciding anything$qb$, $qb$Explain why you think it is a waste of time$qb$, $qb$Do it and raise your view afterwards$qb$, $qb$Do it in the quickest way possible$qb$, $qb$Ask whether someone else could do it instead$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably keeps a manager informed without taking up her time?$qb$, $qb$A short regular update she can read when she chooses$qb$, $qb$Telling her whenever something significant happens$qb$, $qb$A weekly meeting to go through progress$qb$, $qb$Copying her into the relevant messages$qb$, $qb$Answering fully whenever she asks$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager has asked for something by Friday and you can see it will take until Tuesday. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say so today and ask what can move$qb$, $qb$Give her Tuesday as the date and explain the reason$qb$, $qb$Deliver what you can by Friday and the rest after$qb$, $qb$Work extra hours to make Friday$qb$, $qb$Wait until Thursday and see how close you are$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have an idea that would improve your team's work. What is most useful when raising it?$qb$, $qb$What it would change for the things your manager is measured on$qb$, $qb$How the idea would work in practice$qb$, $qb$What it would cost to try$qb$, $qb$Why the current way is a problem$qb$, $qb$How long it would take to put in place$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager rarely gives feedback. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Ask about one specific piece of work rather than in general$qb$, $qb$Ask her for feedback on your performance$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague how your work is seen$qb$, $qb$Wait for the formal review$qb$, $qb$Assume no news means the work is acceptable$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the most useful thing to establish when two managers give you conflicting instructions?$qb$, $qb$Which of them is accountable for the outcome$qb$, $qb$The seniority of the two managers$qb$, $qb$Which instruction came first$qb$, $qb$How urgent each instruction is$qb$, $qb$Whichever of them is easier to go back to$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your manager makes a decision based on a fact you know is out of date. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Give her the current figure straight away$qb$, $qb$Ask where the figure came from$qb$, $qb$Mention that the figure may have changed$qb$, $qb$Let the decision stand and correct the record later$qb$, $qb$Say nothing, since the decision is hers to make$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What usually makes a manager stop trusting someone's estimates?$qb$, $qb$The estimates are met only by cutting something unseen$qb$, $qb$They change after they have been given$qb$, $qb$They turn out to be wrong more often than not$qb$, $qb$The person always estimates the same length$qb$, $qb$The person never asks for more time$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at a hardware shop. Your manager has told you to serve customers first and the owner has told you to finish the stock count today. Both are in the shop this morning. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Say to both together that one has to give way, and ask which$qb$, $qb$Ask your manager how to handle the owner's instruction$qb$, $qb$Serve customers and count stock between them$qb$, $qb$Do the stock count, since the owner asked for it$qb$, $qb$Serve customers, since that is your manager's instruction$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a cloth shop. Your manager has asked for the new stock to be displayed by Saturday. The supplier has just told you delivery will arrive Monday. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell her today that Saturday is not possible and what the options are$qb$, $qb$Tell her today that the delivery has slipped to Monday$qb$, $qb$Ask the supplier whether Saturday is still possible$qb$, $qb$Display what you already have and add the new stock later$qb$, $qb$Wait until Saturday and explain then$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You supervise a staff canteen. Your manager wants the menu shortened to save cost. You know the two dishes she wants removed are the ones most staff come for. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Show her what those two dishes bring in before the menu changes$qb$, $qb$Tell her those two dishes are the most popular$qb$, $qb$Ask her which cost she is trying to bring down$qb$, $qb$Remove them and see how staff react$qb$, $qb$Remove them, since the instruction is clear$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a car wash. Your manager has set a target of forty vehicles a day. Your two machines can handle thirty at the current wash setting. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell her what forty would need and let her choose$qb$, $qb$Tell her that forty is not achievable with two machines$qb$, $qb$Ask her whether the wash setting can be shortened$qb$, $qb$Aim for forty and reduce the wash time to fit$qb$, $qb$Do thirty and report the shortfall each day$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work on a poultry farm. Your manager has asked you to move a delivery to Thursday. The birds will not be ready until Friday. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell her today what Thursday would mean for the birds$qb$, $qb$Tell her the birds will not be ready until Friday$qb$, $qb$Ask her why the delivery needs to move$qb$, $qb$Move the delivery and send whatever is ready$qb$, $qb$Wait until Thursday and tell her then that the birds are not ready$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a milk booth. Your manager has told you to open at five and the society has told you to open at six. You cannot do both and you have not raised it. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Put both opening times to your manager and ask which one stands$qb$, $qb$Ask the society to put their instruction in writing$qb$, $qb$Open at five, since your manager is the one who supervises you$qb$, $qb$Open at six and explain to your manager if she asks$qb$, $qb$Alternate between the two times until someone notices$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at a photo framing shop. Your manager gives you the day's jobs each morning but never says which are urgent. You have guessed wrong twice this month. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Ask her each morning which jobs must go out that day$qb$, $qb$Ask her to mark the urgent jobs when she hands them over$qb$, $qb$Ask her why the urgent ones are not identified$qb$, $qb$Order the jobs by customer promise date yourself$qb$, $qb$Continue as you are, since only two have gone wrong$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a vegetable market stall. Your manager has asked for a full stock list by noon each day. It takes you an hour, which is your busiest trading hour. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Explain the lost trade caused by doing the list at noon and propose another time for her approval.$qb$, $qb$Tell her that completing the list at noon conflicts with serving customers during the busiest hour.$qb$, $qb$Ask her what the list is used for$qb$, $qb$Do the list at noon and accept the lost trade$qb$, $qb$Do the list after trading and date it as noon$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work in a furniture showroom. Your manager has promised a customer delivery on Tuesday without checking with you. The item is not in stock. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell her today what is possible so she can go back to the customer$qb$, $qb$Tell her the item is not in stock$qb$, $qb$Ask her when she promised the customer$qb$, $qb$Contact the customer yourself and change the date$qb$, $qb$Order the item and hope it arrives by Tuesday$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-SJT-046$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at a gas agency. Your manager has asked you to take on the evening round as well as your morning one. You can do both only by shortening the safety checks. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Say plainly what would have to be cut, and let her decide$qb$, $qb$Ask her which of the two rounds matters more$qb$, $qb$Suggest another person takes the evening round instead$qb$, $qb$Take both rounds and do the checks more quickly$qb$, $qb$Take both rounds and raise it if something goes wrong$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-SAM-SJT-047$qb$, $qb$A1-05$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You work at a fertiliser depot. Your manager asks each week how the stock is moving. Your answers have been rough figures. She has now used one of them in a report. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Give her the accurate figure now and say the earlier one was rough$qb$, $qb$Tell her the figures you gave were approximate$qb$, $qb$Check the accurate figure before saying anything$qb$, $qb$Let the report stand and give better figures in future$qb$, $qb$Say nothing, since the rough figure was close enough$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
