  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-FIB-015$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$The person who demands certainty before starting will start ______.$qb$, $qb$last$qb$, $qb$twice$qb$, $qb$cheaply$qb$, $qb$quietly$qb$, $qb$alone$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-FIB-016$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$An unclear brief is better handled by producing something to ______ than by waiting.$qb$, $qb$react to$qb$, $qb$pay for$qb$, $qb$file$qb$, $qb$insure$qb$, $qb$publish$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-FIB-017$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$FIB$qb$, $qb$Two possible futures are easier to prepare for than one that is merely ______.$qb$, $qb$assumed$qb$, $qb$costly$qb$, $qb$distant$qb$, $qb$public$qb$, $qb$seasonal$qb$, 5, 0, 0, 0, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-018$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your goals have changed twice this month and may change again. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Find the part of the work that holds whichever way it goes$qb$, $qb$Ask for the goals to be settled before continuing$qb$, $qb$Work to the most recent version until told otherwise$qb$, $qb$Wait until the goals stop changing$qb$, $qb$Work to the original goals, since they may return$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-019$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have been asked to start something with only half the requirements known. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Build the part that is certain and leave the rest open$qb$, $qb$Make reasonable assumptions and record them$qb$, $qb$Ask for the remaining requirements first$qb$, $qb$Start on the part you find most interesting$qb$, $qb$Wait until the requirements are complete$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-020$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most helps a team keep working while a restructure is being decided?$qb$, $qb$Knowing which of their work is unaffected$qb$, $qb$Being told the restructure will be announced soon$qb$, $qb$Being kept informed of the discussions$qb$, $qb$Being reassured about their own positions$qb$, $qb$Being given more work to occupy them$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-021$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A colleague keeps asking for certainty you cannot give. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Tell her what is settled and what is genuinely open$qb$, $qb$Give your best estimate of what will happen$qb$, $qb$Ask her to wait until there is more information$qb$, $qb$Tell her you do not know either$qb$, $qb$Tell her not to worry about it$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-022$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have said out loud that you are unsure about something. What does this usually buy you?$qb$, $qb$People bring you the doubts they were holding back$qb$, $qb$People understand why the decision took time$qb$, $qb$People stop expecting a firm answer$qb$, $qb$People lose some confidence in your judgement$qb$, $qb$People make their own decisions instead$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-023$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your project's direction may change in two months. What kind of work should you do now?$qb$, $qb$Work that is useful under either direction$qb$, $qb$Anything that can be finished inside two months$qb$, $qb$Whatever the current direction requires$qb$, $qb$Preparation for the direction you think likelier$qb$, $qb$Tasks that could be paused if things change$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-024$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team knows a change is coming and has been given no detail at all. What are they most likely to do?$qb$, $qb$Fill the gap with their own worst guesses$qb$, $qb$Wait quietly until more is known$qb$, $qb$Slow down on work that may be wasted$qb$, $qb$Ask around for information elsewhere$qb$, $qb$Carry on as though nothing were changing$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-025$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You are given an unclear brief and cannot reach the person who wrote it. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Produce a rough version they can correct$qb$, $qb$Write down your reading and start on that$qb$, $qb$Ask a colleague how they read it$qb$, $qb$Do the parts that are clear and leave the rest$qb$, $qb$Wait until you can reach them$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-026$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most reliably keeps a decision reversible while things are unclear?$qb$, $qb$Choosing the option that closes fewest doors$qb$, $qb$Making the decision for a fixed period only$qb$, $qb$Keeping the decision informal$qb$, $qb$Telling fewer people about it$qb$, $qb$Documenting why it was made$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-027$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two of your team react very differently to the same uncertainty. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Give each of them the kind of anchor they need$qb$, $qb$Treat them the same to be fair$qb$, $qb$Explain the situation to both again$qb$, $qb$Pair them so one steadies the other$qb$, $qb$Give the more anxious one less to worry about$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-028$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A senior manager asks for a firm forecast in a situation you cannot forecast. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Give a range and say what would move it$qb$, $qb$Give your best single figure$qb$, $qb$Explain why a forecast is not possible$qb$, $qb$Ask what the forecast will be used for$qb$, $qb$Give a cautious figure you are confident of$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-029$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What distinguishes useful patience from simply waiting?$qb$, $qb$Something is being learned while you wait$qb$, $qb$The waiting has a fixed end point$qb$, $qb$The delay has been agreed with others$qb$, $qb$You are ready to move when it clears$qb$, $qb$The alternative would be worse$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-030$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Your team's structure is about to change and nobody knows how. What is most useful now?$qb$, $qb$Keep the work going and name what will not change$qb$, $qb$Tell the team what you know and what you do not$qb$, $qb$Ask senior management for a date$qb$, $qb$Reassure the team about their roles$qb$, $qb$Pause new work until the structure settles$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-031$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You must commit to a supplier before you know the volume you will need. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Commit to the minimum and keep the option to add$qb$, $qb$Commit to your best estimate of the volume$qb$, $qb$Delay the commitment as long as possible$qb$, $qb$Commit to a high volume to secure supply$qb$, $qb$Ask the supplier to hold the price open$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-032$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What is the main cost of demanding full information before acting?$qb$, $qb$The situation changes while you are gathering it$qb$, $qb$The gathering itself takes resources$qb$, $qb$Others make the decision instead$qb$, $qb$You appear indecisive$qb$, $qb$The information may never be complete$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-033$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A market you serve is changing in a way nobody understands yet. What is most useful?$qb$, $qb$Run two small bets rather than one large one$qb$, $qb$Study the change before committing anything$qb$, $qb$Follow whichever competitor moves first$qb$, $qb$Stay as you are until the change is clear$qb$, $qb$Commit early to gain the advantage$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-034$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$You have been given a role whose boundaries nobody can define. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Start where the need is clearest and let the shape follow$qb$, $qb$Ask for the boundaries to be written down$qb$, $qb$Define the boundaries yourself and propose them$qb$, $qb$Do what your predecessor did until told otherwise$qb$, $qb$Wait until the role becomes clearer$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-035$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$What most helps someone stay effective when priorities keep shifting?$qb$, $qb$Knowing which things must not slip whatever else changes$qb$, $qb$Being told about changes as early as possible$qb$, $qb$Having fewer priorities at any one time$qb$, $qb$Being given time to adjust after each change$qb$, $qb$Understanding why the priorities keep changing$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-MCQ-036$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A situation has become clearer and your earlier view now looks wrong. What is best?$qb$, $qb$Say what has changed and what you now think$qb$, $qb$Adjust your position without drawing attention$qb$, $qb$Wait until it is clearer still before changing$qb$, $qb$Explain why the earlier view was reasonable$qb$, $qb$Hold the earlier view until it is proved wrong$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-SJT-037$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage an accountancy office. New reporting rules have been announced but the detail will not be published for three months. Clients are asking what to do. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell clients what is settled, what is not, and what you will do at each point$qb$, $qb$Give clients your best reading of what the rules will require$qb$, $qb$Tell clients the detail is not yet published$qb$, $qb$Advise clients to wait until the detail is published$qb$, $qb$Prepare clients for the strictest possible version$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-SJT-038$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a customs clearing office. A shipment's classification is disputed and could go either way. The client needs to plan. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Set out both outcomes and what each would mean for his plans$qb$, $qb$Tell him the classification is still disputed$qb$, $qb$Give him the outcome you think more likely$qb$, $qb$Advise him to wait for the ruling$qb$, $qb$Plan on the outcome that costs him least$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-SJT-039$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You repair musical instruments. A customer's instrument has a fault you cannot yet identify and he needs it for a performance in ten days. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Tell him what you have ruled out and agree a point to decide$qb$, $qb$Tell him you have not yet found the fault$qb$, $qb$Give him your best guess at what it is$qb$, $qb$Ask him to leave it with you until you know$qb$, $qb$Suggest he borrows an instrument for the performance$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-SJT-040$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a plumbing supplies wholesaler. A manufacturer may or may not discontinue a line you sell heavily. Nothing has been confirmed. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Hold enough stock to cover either outcome and watch for the signal$qb$, $qb$Ask the manufacturer for a firm answer$qb$, $qb$Stock up heavily in case it is discontinued$qb$, $qb$Find an alternative supplier now$qb$, $qb$Carry on as normal until something is confirmed$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-SJT-041$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage a carpet showroom. Your head office has announced a change of range but has not said which lines go. Customers are ordering. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Keep selling and tell customers which lines you can still guarantee$qb$, $qb$Tell customers the range is changing$qb$, $qb$Stop taking orders until the range is confirmed$qb$, $qb$Sell only from lines you think will survive$qb$, $qb$Take orders and deal with any problems later$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-SJT-042$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a kitchen fitting company. A client keeps changing the layout and may change it again before you start. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Begin the work that is the same under every layout so far$qb$, $qb$Ask the client to confirm the layout before you start$qb$, $qb$Start on the current layout and adjust as needed$qb$, $qb$Wait until the client stops changing it$qb$, $qb$Price the job to cover repeated changes$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-SJT-043$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a signwriting workshop. A festival has booked you but cannot confirm the site until a week before. Your work needs three weeks. How do you handle it?$qb$, $qb$Make everything that does not depend on the site now$qb$, $qb$Ask the festival to confirm the site sooner$qb$, $qb$Start on your best guess at the site$qb$, $qb$Wait for the site and warn them the work may not be ready$qb$, $qb$Decline the booking, since the timing does not work$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-SJT-044$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run a leather goods workshop. A buyer may place a large order but will not say when or how large. Your workshop is quiet. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Take other work you can pause or finish quickly$qb$, $qb$Ask the buyer for an indication of size and timing$qb$, $qb$Keep capacity free in case the order comes$qb$, $qb$Take other work and turn the buyer down if it clashes$qb$, $qb$Wait for the buyer, since the order would be large$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
  ($qb$HEAIL-TOA-SJT-045$qb$, $qb$A1-02$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You manage an optical frame factory. A design may be adopted by a large retailer or may not. Tooling takes six weeks and is expensive. How do you decide?$qb$, $qb$Tool only the parts the design shares with your existing range$qb$, $qb$Ask the retailer for a decision before tooling$qb$, $qb$Tool now so you are ready if they adopt it$qb$, $qb$Wait for the decision and accept the six-week delay$qb$, $qb$Decline unless the retailer commits first$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
