  ($qb$HEAIL-HAI-SJT-050$qb$, $qb$A1-01$qb$, $qb$SJT$qb$, $qb$You run an archive digitisation unit. A tool reads old handwriting well. On pages where the ink has faded it still produces a reading, with no sign that it was uncertain. How do you respond?$qb$, $qb$Flag the faded pages so their readings are not trusted equally$qb$, $qb$Have a person re-read the faded pages$qb$, $qb$Record which pages were faded and leave the readings as they are$qb$, $qb$Accept the readings, since the tool is usually accurate$qb$, $qb$Leave the faded pages out of the archive altogether$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true)
